# nerima-lisp standard .gitignore
# Copy to <repo>/.gitignore and append repository-specific entries below the
# marked section. Everything above the marker must stay identical across repos
# so that "is this artifact ignored?" has the same answer everywhere.

# --- Common Lisp build output ---
*.fasl
*.fas
*.lib
*.dfsl
*.ufsl
*.fsl

# --- Nix ---
/result
/result-*
/.direnv/

# --- Test and coverage output ---
/coverage/
/coverage-report/
/*-coverage-report/
*.coverage
coverage.dat
/__snapshots__/
/*-snapshots/

# --- Local caches and scratch space ---
/.cache/
/.deps/
/tmp/
/.worktrees/
/.paredit.cleanup/

# --- Credentials ---
# Not because anyone plans to put a key here, but because the cost of the one
# time it happens by accident is a rotation across the whole org. See
# SUPPLY_CHAIN.md for what to do if one is committed anyway.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
/secrets/

# --- Editor and OS noise ---
.DS_Store
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# --- Repository-specific entries below this line ---

# Fasl extensions for the non-SBCL implementations this repository's previous
# .gitignore covered. The shared block above lists the SBCL/CMUCL/CLISP set;
# these are CCL's and ABCL's, kept so the migration does not start tracking
# build output that used to be ignored here.
*.lx64fsl
*.lx32fsl
*.dx64fsl
*.dx32fsl
*.abcl

# ASDF system index caches (written next to the .asd by some ASDF versions).
system-index.txt

# clweb tangle/weave output for the literate contrib (regenerate from *.clw).
/contrib/literate/*.lisp
/contrib/literate/*.tex

# MkDocs build output. site_dir is ../site, so this lands at the repo root
# (regenerate with `mkdocs build -f docs/mkdocs.yml`).
/site/

# Saved cores and executables. `cl-tty-kit` is the name a saved core would
# take, and it collides with cl-tty-kit.asd only by prefix, so the negation
# below keeps the system definition tracked.
*.core
/cl-tty-kit
!cl-tty-kit.asd

# Local tool state (Serena semantic index and caches).
/.serena/
